{
  "version": 2,
  "name": "Water — Dam Break (Live GPU)",
  "description": "GPU MLS-MPM dam break: the Water — Dam Break column and basin simulated live on the GPU, one fixed 60 Hz tick per frame. The solver is one group, Live Matter: the domain sets the lattice, walls, gravity and clock; the fill seeds points; Point State repeats Clear Grid, Points To Grid, Grid Update and Grid To Points once per substep; Tick Stats checks each tick; Frame publishes the particles. The group flattens to the same graph as its wired atoms. Particles are drawn as small spheres until the liquid surface lands.",
